# why: The remote's arrows did nothing in bubbles and dialogs, and on chrome://history neither Up nor Back responded.
# - Bubbles and dialogs ("Bookmark added", the profile menu, permission prompts) are widgets of their own, outside the
#   browser window's key handler (patch 0017), and views moves focus there only with Tab. One aura::Env handler now
#   moves focus with the arrows in any dialog widget: Up/Left back, Down/Right forward; text fields keep Left/Right
#   until the caret is at the end; web contents in a bubble and open menus keep their keys.
# - chrome://history's list keeps Up at its first row, and the page takes Escape (Back) to clear its selection. On
#   chrome:// pages Up/Down now run our spatial navigation first, and Back closes a dialog or menu open in the page,
#   else goes back (patch 0057). While a text field has focus the page gets its keys first, as before.
# - The navigation script looks one screen beyond the visible part for Up/Down (long lists scroll with the focus) and
#   stays inside an open dialog or menu.
